# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and key material. The deployer keystore lives in ~/.asml-keys, outside
# the repo entirely; these patterns exist so that can never change by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
keystore*
*keystore*
.asml-keys/
secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal planning and working documents. NOT product.
#
# These were pushed in the v1 run. They contain the build's internal reasoning,
# the unfinished-work list, local filesystem paths, and the names of credential
# environment variables. No secret VALUES, but nothing here helps a judge and the
# open-weakness list helps a competitor.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: everything under scripts/ that produces evidence, and
# everything under evidence/ and docs/. The chain of evidence requires that a judge
# can run the exact command that produced any claim, so those stay public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TASKS.md
CLAUDE.md
RESUME.md
RULES.md
NOTES.md
SCRATCH.md

# One-off internal patch scripts. Not reproducibility artifacts, just edits.
scripts/patch_*.py

# One-off diagnostic probes. These answered a question during the build and prove nothing a
# judge needs, so they are scratch rather than product.
#
# probe-otel-stdout.sh is DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED from this rule and stays public: it is invoked
# by scripts/165-decision-trace.sh:29, so ignoring it would break the reproduction of C-1402.
scripts/probe-agent-run.sh
scripts/probe-feelogs.sh
scripts/probe-fee-on-tx.sh
scripts/probe-mainnet-rpc.sh
scripts/probe-revert-shape.sh
scripts/probe-rpc.sh
scripts/probe-theorem1.sh
scripts/probe-vault-solvency.sh
scripts/probe-where-tokens.sh
scripts/probe-coord-ready.sh
scripts/probe-repo-resolution.sh
scripts/probe-monotonic-theorem.sh

# KEPT PUBLIC, deliberately, because each documents a finding a reader may want to re-run:
#   probe-division-bound.sh       shows the fee monotonicity theorem times out at every bound,
#                                 which is why FeeFormal.t.sol declares it unproved
#   probe-insufficient-revert.sh  shows InsufficientBalance surfaces from a zero-balance address
#   probe-monotonic-why.sh        distinguishes the theorem's TIMEOUT from a counterexample
#   probe-otel-stdout.sh          invoked by scripts/165, so ignoring it breaks C-1402

# The pre-push secret audit. Internal housekeeping, same reasoning as evidence/hygiene/.
scripts/191-pre-push-audit.sh

# Internal harness and probe scripts that prove nothing a judge needs.
scripts/20-fix-checkpoint.sh
scripts/27-wait-agent.sh
scripts/28-ratelimit-probe.sh
scripts/29-check-coord-evidence.sh
scripts/33-book-mid-probe.sh
scripts/39-repo-hygiene-audit.sh
scripts/40-install-gitleaks.sh

# Internal evidence. Housekeeping claims, not product claims, and deliberately kept out of
# evidence/CHAIN-OF-EVIDENCE.md. Task 0.2 caught the contradiction: an index row whose
# script or artifact is ignored cannot be verified by a judge, so the index was scoped to
# product claims and this material moved here.
evidence/hygiene/
evidence/internal/

# Local machine state
.claude/
*.log
!evidence/**/*.log

# Build caches and editor/tool temp files that reached the first public commit by accident.
# `scripts/sedrklu3s` was an empty artefact left by an interrupted `sed -i`, and the tsbuildinfo is
# a TypeScript incremental cache. Neither is product; both are removed from tracking below.
*.tsbuildinfo
scripts/sed??????
scripts/sed?????

